# Round XII Track R — REJECT `Mutex[Trait]` at CALL-EXPRESSION generic-arg
# position, `.get()`-chained variant. Sibling of
# `mutex_bare_trait_chained_call_reject.gg` — the intermediate `.get()` hop
# had exposed a DIFFERENT link-time symptom pre-Track-R (fabricated
# `int64_t__greet` at ld time, Round XI Track M class 3), but Track R's
# reject fires on the CALLEE (`Mutex`) before typecheck ever inspects the
# `.lock().get().greet()` chain, so both variants collapse to the same
# check-time reject. Kept as a distinct axis-cell fixture so a partial
# regression on the chain-shape (removing `.get()` from the up-front
# reject's early-return) would still trip a fixture rather than silently
# accept the `.get()`-shape.
#
# Reject fires at the callee span (`Mutex` identifier); user is advised to
# write `Mutex[Box[Speaker]]` (D36, `docs/define-gorget/decisions.md:1403`).

trait Speaker:
    String greet(self)

struct Robot:
    String name

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String greet(self):
        return "beep " + self.name

void main():
    print(Mutex[Speaker](Robot("R2")).lock().get().greet())
